  "rationale": "No single non-foothold step is a chokepoint, because the target can be reached by two routes that share no intermediate step. Route A: iotDevice:exploitPublicApp -> memoryDump:credentialAccess -> printServer:lateralMovement -> mailArchive:collection or vaultRead:collection -> target. Route B: containerHost:exploitPublicApp -> configSecret:credentialAccess -> appServer:lateralMovement -> vaultRead:collection -> target. vaultRead appears in both, but blocking it still leaves mailArchive in Route A. appServer is also reachable through dbLogin, since dmzWeb and kerberoast are both reachable. Blocking any step in one route leaves the other route intact, so the target stays reachable."
